    {
      "id": "heek67q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Science and Technology"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gtntjv6",
      "content": "• Aryabhata discovered that the Earth rotates on its axis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hvvw9yb",
      "content": "• The concept of zero was developed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l6vznqt",
      "content": "• Advancements were made in astronomy and mathematics."
    },
    {
      "id": "qwdxl4b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Decline of the Gupta Empire"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "76a45of",
      "content": "• Weak successors after Skandagupta."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Remember the exact reign dates: Samudragupta (335–375 CE) and Chandragupta II (380–415 CE).",
        "Chandragupta II is directly identified with the title 'Vikramaditya' in competitive exams.",
        "Key topics frequently tested include Gupta administration, literature, and contributions to science and technology."
      ],
      "id": "2gf4vls"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ahiwlel",
      "content": "• Hun invasions weakened the empire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o60t3mo",
      "content": "• Economic problems and administrative weaknesses."
    },
    {
      "id": "xzifge3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SSC Exam Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nqoxpuo",
      "content": "• The Gupta period is known as the Golden Age of Ancient India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aytb4ko",
      "content": "• Samudragupta is called the Napoleon of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w1ufm3j",
      "content": "• Fa-Hien visited India during Chandragupta II's reign."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "edayije",
      "content": "• Gold coins of the Guptas were called Dinaras."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y9slyr2",
      "content": "• Aryabhata was a famous scientist of the Gupta period."
    }
